{
  "id": "cda50609-0c44-4008-b801-404bce7aaf5f",
  "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
  "data": {
    "body": "Assume that all vectors and subspaces are in $\\mathbb{R}^{n}$. Which of the following statements is FALSE?",
    "solution": [
      0
    ],
    "answerChoices": [
      {
        "id": "599af445-b72f-4def-8ae6-357eb807d56b",
        "index": 0,
        "body": "The best approximation to $\\mathbf{y}$ by elements of a subspace $W$ is the vector $\\mathbf{y}-\\operatorname{proj}_{W} \\mathbf{y}$",
        "questionId": "cda50609-0c44-4008-b801-404bce7aaf5f",
        "stats": {
          "count": 2491
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "0d5dc6e2-3170-4570-98f2-2d853d1dbd33",
        "index": 1,
        "body": "If $\\mathbf{z}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{u}_{\\mathbf{1}}$ and $\\mathbf{u}_{\\mathbf{2}}$, and if $W=\\operatorname{Span}\\left\\{\\mathbf{u}_{\\mathbf{1}}, \\mathbf{u}_{\\mathbf{2}}\\right\\}$, then $\\mathbf{z}$ is in $W^{\\perp}$.",
        "questionId": "cda50609-0c44-4008-b801-404bce7aaf5f",
        "stats": {
          "count": 239
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "f3c4790d-26c2-4ab3-9362-92d37ea5ba09",
        "index": 2,
        "body": "If $\\mathbf{y}=\\mathbf{z}_{\\mathbf{1}}+\\mathbf{z}_{\\mathbf{2}}$, where $\\mathbf{z}_{\\mathbf{1}}$ is in a subspace $W$ and $\\mathbf{z}_{\\mathbf{2}}$ is in $W^{\\perp}$, then $\\operatorname{proj}_{W} \\mathbf{y}=\\mathbf{z}_{\\mathbf{1}}$.",
        "questionId": "cda50609-0c44-4008-b801-404bce7aaf5f",
        "stats": {
          "count": 857
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "da2db9be-81f6-43b1-9361-697f7047d143",
        "index": 3,
        "body": "If $\\mathbf{x}$ is not in a subspace $W$, then $\\mathbf{x}-\\operatorname{proj}_{W} \\mathbf{x}$ is not zero.",
        "questionId": "cda50609-0c44-4008-b801-404bce7aaf5f",
        "stats": {
          "count": 611
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "a38c5671-97b0-4435-9191-26a8074c762a",
        "index": 4,
        "body": "If the columns of an $m \\times n$ matrix $A$ are orthonormal, then the linear mapping $\\mathbf{x} \\mapsto A \\mathbf{x}$ preserves length.",
        "questionId": "cda50609-0c44-4008-b801-404bce7aaf5f",
        "stats": {
          "count": 463
        },
        "resources": []
      }
    ]
